<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Reference on kevin</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/</link><description>Recent content in Reference on kevin</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>CEL expressions</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/cel-expressions/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/cel-expressions/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="cel-expressions"&gt;CEL expressions&lt;a class="anchor" href="#cel-expressions"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Any &lt;code&gt;${...}&lt;/code&gt; inside a step&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;with&lt;/code&gt; block string is evaluated as&#10;&lt;a href="https://cel.dev"&gt;CEL&lt;/a&gt; and spliced back in; a string with no &lt;code&gt;${&lt;/code&gt; is&#10;untouched, and more than one &lt;code&gt;${...}&lt;/code&gt; per string is fine, evaluated left to&#10;right. This page covers the four variables kevin exposes; for the language&#10;itself (operators, &lt;code&gt;has()&lt;/code&gt;, ternary &lt;code&gt;? :&lt;/code&gt;, string/list/map methods), see the&#10;&lt;a href="https://github.com/google/cel-spec/blob/master/doc/langdef.md"&gt;CEL language definition&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kubeconfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${needs.cluster.out.kubeconfig}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;registry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${has(env.REGISTRY_HOST) ? env.REGISTRY_HOST : &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;localhost:5000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="variables"&gt;Variables&lt;a class="anchor" href="#variables"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Four top-level scopes: &lt;a href="#needs"&gt;&lt;code&gt;needs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="#setup"&gt;&lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="#env"&gt;&lt;code&gt;env&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;,&#10;&lt;a href="#project"&gt;&lt;code&gt;project&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>